speechtext:
It being six o'clock, pursuant to Standing Order 13(4)(a), the House will now proceed with the deferred division on the amendment to the amendment of Mr. Cassidy. The question is as follows. Mr. Cassidy, seconded by Mr. Murphy, moved:
That the amendment be amended by adding immediately thereafter the following words:
and this House further condemns the Government for introducing a budget that tolerates the existence of 1,250,000 unemployed Canadians and fails to show fairness to the average Canadian family and regions that continue to feel the burden of economic recession with respect to employment and income;
-for failing to introduce a system of universal childcare that would assist families and create jobs;
-for failing to demonstrate to the average Canadian taxpayer a genuine commitment to tax reform by eliminating in this budget some of the worst excesses in the tax system, such as the erosion of the corporate tax base begun by the Liberals in 1983;
-for failing to even give mention in the budget to the tragedy of 4,000,000 Canadians living in poverty; and
-for failing to make full employment the first priority of the federal government.
